span style=3D"font-weight:700">Good morning, world. </span><span>My mum was=
 the first in her family to attend university. Her grandfather had been a f=
armer, her father a carpenter. She became an engineer. Education, she alway=
s told me, had given her wings.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px=
 georgia,serif;color:#333;margin:0 0 15px"><span>This postwar experience of=
 education being an engine of social mobility was common for members of her=
 generation. It has been a central tenet of the social contract in countrie=
s around the world: If you study hard, you and your children will be better=
 off. But that promise no longer holds in the same way. Today, my colleague=
 Amanda Taub writes about what has gone wrong, and why this moment is so vo=
latile as a result.</span></p><p style=3D"font:normal 17px/25px georgia,ser=
